, {"ref": "BomRef.5631861239488712.08899701389765913"}], "metadata": {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T10:35:17.750564+00:00"}, "serialNumber": "urn:uuid:1eebf99b-ad5d-4c9a-864a-4ae453be0fbe", "version": 1, "vulnerabilities": [{"affects": [{"ref": "BomRef.07791095063256093.10493767614762162"}], "bom-ref": "BomRef.7484058873374018.6568564590701438", "description": "### Summary  On Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's `.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel installation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested `destination_eggdir`.  The attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of the created file.  ### Details  Tested setuptools commit:  `6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`  Relevant source:  `setuptools/wheel.py`  SHA-256:  `359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`  The relevant call path is:  `Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)` \u2192 `_install_as_egg` \u2192 `_convert_metadata` \u2192 `_fix_namespace_packages`  A wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:  `<distribution>.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`  The namespace value is eventually used approximately as:  ```python mod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.')) mod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')  If mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots, mod.split('.') preserves it as a single component. On Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards the original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute path. The existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this metadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.  ```markdown ### PoC  The reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary directory.  Layout:  ```text sandbox/     destination/     outside/     input/     canary.txt ```  A synthetic wheel was created containing:  `demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`  whose content was the absolute path of:  `sandbox\\outside`  The real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:  ```python setuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(     sandbox_destination ) ```  The operation completed without exception.  Expected metadata was created under:  `sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`  but setuptools also created:  `sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`  The file did not exist before execution.  Its contents were:  ```python __import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__) ```  The unrelated canary remained byte-identical.  The sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence. ```   ### Impact  A crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content `__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a filesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the process performing the installation.  The demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to already exist.", "id": "GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w", "recommendation": "Upgrade"}], "$schema": "http://cyclonedx.org/schema/bom-1.4.schema.json", "bomFormat": "CycloneDX", "specVersion": "1.4"}
